=== 7. smallest-safe repair contract (discussion, no choice by convenience) ===
(a) Dependency-correct matched rebuild: rebuild EVERY object whose .deps Tpo binds
    cktdefs.h (1085 objects) against the applied header, then re-archive and re-link.
    Scope: the whole dependency cone of the struct change (deterministic; the retained
    Makefiles drive it via the newer cktdefs.h mtime). Reproducibility: exact (same
    configured tree, same commands, same objects as the accepted flow - the mixed ABI
    is eliminated because no old-layout object survives). Safe: preserves the proven
    V4/V5 design (validated through syntax, object, link, and the control's exact
    reproduction); the repair is re-running the accepted pipeline with the dependency
    discipline the task's LINK flow omitted.
(b) Context design that does not change the shared structure: move the diagnostic
    context OUT of CKTcircuit (revert the struct to the original layout; hold the
    context in a non-struct mechanism - file-static or pointer-keyed registry - with
    the niiter/vbicload referencing it directly or via a tiny accessor). Scope: 3
    files (cktdefs.h revert + niiter.c + vbicload.c) - the smallest FILE set, and it
    eliminates the whole class of mixed-layout ABI risk for any future consumer of
    CKTcircuit. Reproducibility: exact (deterministic builds), but the new mechanism
    needs its own validation (syntax/object/link plus a matched runtime pair).
    Recommendation (criteria: smallest SAFE + reproducibility): (a) is the smallest
    SAFE repair - it reuses the fully validated design and turns the mixed ABI into a
    pure rebuild-discipline fix; (b) is the smallest FILE-set change and the more
    future-proof design but introduces a new mechanism that must be validated from
    scratch. Both are reproducible; the choice is a scope-vs-future-risk trade, not a
    convenience choice.

